  "id": "thalamic-lesion",
  "term": "thalamic lesion",
  "definition": "A thalamic lesion is damage to the thalamus, such as from a stroke affecting this deep brain structure. In the supplied source, bilateral thalamic injury was linked with cognitive impairment marked by executive dysfunction, reduced self-awareness, and mood changes such as apathy and depression.",
